# Bark-Knuckle Boxer: mana a player spends assisting another player's spell (CR 702.132a) is not mana they spent to
# cast spells, so it counts toward nobody's expend (CR 700.14; the user's ruling: only the caster casts the spell, and
# the caster counts only their own mana). On turn 5 Bot1 casts Charging Binox and Bot2, who controls the Boxer, pays {2}
# of it: the Boxer does not trigger. Still in that turn Bot2 casts Shock (its own mana 1), Think Twice (2-3) and Giant
# Growth (4): the Boxer gains indestructible only at Giant Growth, the fourth mana Bot2 itself spent to cast. Counting
# the assist would make Think Twice (2 + 3 = 5) expend 4 instead.

